# secrets
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# data — never commit datasets or transcripts.
# Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `data/` also matches the source package
# `ml/lighthouse/data/`, which silently drops real code from the repo.
/data/

# model artifacts
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
checkpoints/
runs/
artifacts/

# python
.venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# node
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# os / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local scratch. `creds.txt` holds demo counsellor passwords: it is untracked on purpose
# and must stay that way, because this repo goes public before judging.
creds.txt
run.txt
notes.txt
scratch/

# Working documents. These stay on disk because the session workflow in CLAUDE.md reads
# and writes them, but they are not published: log.md is a build diary, submission.md is
# Devpost copy, deploy.md is an operational runbook, and context.md/plan.md are planning
# notes. The four docs that are evidence for the README — architecture, results, ml,
# privacy — are tracked, as are the screenshots.
#
# Note that adding a path here does NOT untrack a file that is already committed, and it
# does not remove it from history. These were purged with `git filter-repo`; if one comes
# back, it needs the same treatment, not just this line.
docs/context.md
docs/plan.md
docs/log.md
docs/ideas.md
docs/improvements.md
docs/deploy.md
docs/demo.md
docs/submission.md
